{"landed-cost": "\n    <h1>Landed Cost Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Find the true cost of an imported part once freight, insurance, duty and customs fees are added. Example values are filled in; replace them with your shipment.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-price\">Unit price (FOB) <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"lc-price\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"4.20\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-qty\">Quantity <span class=\"u\">units</span></label><input id=\"lc-qty\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"5000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-freight\">Freight <span class=\"u\">shipment total</span></label><input id=\"lc-freight\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"1850\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-ins\">Insurance <span class=\"u\">% of goods</span></label><input id=\"lc-ins\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-duty\">Duty rate <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"lc-duty\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"6.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-fees\">Customs &amp; broker fees <span class=\"u\">total</span></label><input id=\"lc-fees\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"320\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"lc-other\">Port, handling, inland <span class=\"u\">total</span></label><input id=\"lc-other\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"410\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label>Duty charged on</label>\n          <div class=\"seg\" id=\"lc-basis\"><button type=\"button\" data-b=\"cif\" aria-pressed=\"true\">CIF value</button><button type=\"button\" data-b=\"fob\" aria-pressed=\"false\">FOB value</button></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Landed cost per unit</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"lc-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"lc-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"lc-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"lc-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"lc-tbl\"></table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><p>Landed cost is everything you pay to get goods onto your shop floor. The purchase price is only the start.</p>\n      <code class=\"fx\">Customs value = goods + freight + insurance  (CIF)\nDuty         = customs value × duty rate\nLanded cost  = goods + freight + insurance\n             + duty + fees + handling</code></div>\n      <div><h2>CIF or FOB?</h2><p>The EU, UK, Korea, China and most other countries charge duty on the CIF value, which includes freight and insurance. The US and Canada charge duty on the FOB value, so freight is left out of the duty base.</p><p>Duty rates come from the HS code of your product. Check your country's tariff schedule before you quote a price.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "cost-per-good-unit": "\n    <h1>Cost per Good Unit Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Every rejected part still used material, labor and machine time. This spreads that cost over the parts you can actually ship.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-mat\">Material cost <span class=\"u\">per unit started</span></label><input id=\"cg-mat\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"2.80\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-conv\">Labor + overhead <span class=\"u\">per unit started</span></label><input id=\"cg-conv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"1.65\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-start\">Units started <span class=\"u\">per batch</span></label><input id=\"cg-start\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"12000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"cg-yield\">First-pass yield <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"cg-yield\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"91.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"cg-salv\">Scrap salvage value <span class=\"u\">per rejected unit</span></label><input id=\"cg-salv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.15\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Cost per good unit</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"cg-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"cg-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"cg-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"cg-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"cg-tbl\"></table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Good units   = units started × yield\nTotal cost   = started × (material + conversion)\n             − rejects × salvage\nCost / good  = total cost ÷ good units</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Why yield matters</h2><p>At 90% yield, each good part carries the cost of about 1.11 parts. Raising yield from 90% to 95% cuts that to 1.05, which lowers unit cost by about 5% without touching material prices.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "scrap-cost": "\n    <h1>Scrap &amp; Rework Cost Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Put a yearly number on quality losses so an improvement project can be justified in money, not percentages.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-vol\">Production volume <span class=\"u\">units / month</span></label><input id=\"sc-vol\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"40000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-cost\">Full cost per unit <span class=\"u\">at scrap point</span></label><input id=\"sc-cost\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"6.40\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-scrap\">Scrap rate <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"sc-scrap\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"3.2\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-salv\">Salvage value <span class=\"u\">per scrapped unit</span></label><input id=\"sc-salv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"0.40\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-rw\">Rework rate <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"sc-rw\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"4.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"sc-rwc\">Rework cost <span class=\"u\">per reworked unit</span></label><input id=\"sc-rwc\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"1.90\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"sc-target\">Target scrap rate after improvement <span class=\"u\">%</span></label><input id=\"sc-target\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"1.5\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Quality loss per year</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"sc-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"sc-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"sc-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"sc-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"sc-tbl\"></table>\n        <div id=\"sc-pill\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Scrap loss  = volume × scrap % × (cost − salvage)\nRework loss = volume × rework % × rework cost\nYearly loss = (scrap + rework) × 12</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Which unit cost to use</h2><p>Use the full cost the part has absorbed at the step where it is scrapped. A part rejected at final inspection carries every operation before it, so it costs more than one rejected at incoming inspection.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "break-even": "\n    <h1>Break-Even Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">How many units you need to sell each month before the product starts making money.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-fixed\">Fixed costs <span class=\"u\">per month</span></label><input id=\"be-fixed\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"28000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-price\">Selling price <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"be-price\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"24\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-var\">Variable cost <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"be-var\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"13.5\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"be-target\">Target profit <span class=\"u\">per month</span></label><input id=\"be-target\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"8000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"be-sales\">Expected sales <span class=\"u\">units / month</span></label><input id=\"be-sales\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"3500\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Break-even volume</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"be-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"be-sub\"></div>\n        <div class=\"bar\" id=\"be-bar\"></div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"be-leg\"></div>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"be-tbl\"></table>\n        <div id=\"be-pill\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Contribution  = price − variable cost\nBreak-even    = fixed costs ÷ contribution\nTarget volume = (fixed + target) ÷ contribution\nSafety margin = (expected − break-even) ÷ expected</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Fixed vs variable</h2><p>Fixed costs stay the same whatever you produce: rent, salaried staff, leases, depreciation. Variable costs rise with each unit: material, piece-rate labor, packaging, sales commission and shipping.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "payback": "\n    <h1>Equipment Payback &amp; ROI Calculator</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Test whether a new machine, fixture or automation cell pays for itself, and how fast.</p>\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <div class=\"fields\">\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-inv\">Investment <span class=\"u\">purchase + install</span></label><input id=\"pb-inv\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"185000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-life\">Useful life <span class=\"u\">years</span></label><input id=\"pb-life\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"7\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-labor\">Labor savings <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"pb-labor\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"52000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-qual\">Scrap / quality savings <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"pb-qual\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"14000\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-op\">Added running cost <span class=\"u\">power, upkeep / year</span></label><input id=\"pb-op\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"9500\"></div>\n        <div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pb-rate\">Discount rate <span class=\"u\">% / year</span></label><input id=\"pb-rate\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" inputmode=\"decimal\" value=\"8\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div class=\"kicker\">Simple payback</div>\n        <div class=\"big\" id=\"pb-out\">–</div>\n        <div class=\"sub\" id=\"pb-sub\"></div>\n        <svg id=\"pb-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 120\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cumulative cash flow by year\" style=\"margin-top:14px;max-width:100%\"></svg>\n        <table class=\"bd\" id=\"pb-tbl\"></table>\n        <div id=\"pb-pill\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Net saving = labor + quality − running cost\nPayback    = investment ÷ net saving\nROI        = (net saving × life − investment)\n             ÷ investment\nNPV        = Σ net saving ÷ (1+r)^t − investment</code></div>\n      <div><h2>Reading the result</h2><p>Many plants approve projects that pay back in under 2–3 years. NPV is the stricter test: a positive NPV means the machine earns more than leaving the money at your discount rate.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  ", "machine-hour-rate": "<h1>Machine Hour Rate Calculator</h1><p class=\"lede\">Work out what one hour of a machine really costs: depreciation, interest on capital, floor space, maintenance and power. Use it to quote jobs and to compare in-house work with subcontracting.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-price\">Machine price <span class=\"u\">installed</span></label><input id=\"mh-price\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"250000\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-resid\">Residual value <span class=\"u\">at end of life</span></label><input id=\"mh-resid\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"25000\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-life\">Useful life <span class=\"u\">years</span></label><input id=\"mh-life\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"10\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-int\">Interest rate <span class=\"u\">% / year</span></label><input id=\"mh-int\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"6\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-hrs\">Hours per shift <span class=\"u\">h</span></label><input id=\"mh-hrs\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"8\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-shifts\">Shifts per day <span class=\"u\"></span></label><input id=\"mh-shifts\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"2\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-days\">Working days <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"mh-days\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"250\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-util\">Utilisation <span class=\"u\">% of available time</span></label><input id=\"mh-util\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"75\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-area\">Floor space <span class=\"u\">m² or ft²</span></label><input id=\"mh-area\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"20\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-rent\">Space cost <span class=\"u\">per m² (or ft²) / year</span></label><input id=\"mh-rent\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"120\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-maint\">Maintenance <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"mh-maint\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"6000\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-kw\">Connected load <span class=\"u\">kW</span></label><input id=\"mh-kw\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"15\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-load\">Average load <span class=\"u\">% of connected</span></label><input id=\"mh-load\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"60\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"mh-elec\">Electricity price <span class=\"u\">per kWh</span></label><input id=\"mh-elec\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0.18\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"mh-wage\">Operator cost <span class=\"u\">per hour, burdened</span></label><input id=\"mh-wage\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"38\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">Machine rate per hour</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"mh-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"mh-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"mh-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"mh-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"mh-tbl\"></table></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Running hours = hours × shifts × days × utilisation\nDepreciation  = (price − residual) ÷ life\nInterest      = (price + residual) ÷ 2 × rate\nFixed / hour  = (depreciation + interest + space\n                + maintenance) ÷ running hours\nEnergy / hour = kW × load × price per kWh\nRate          = fixed / hour + energy / hour</code></div><div><h2>Why utilisation matters</h2><p>Fixed costs are spread over the hours the machine actually runs. Halving utilisation doubles the fixed cost per hour, which is why an idle machine is expensive even when it is paid off.</p></div></div>", "oee": "<h1>OEE Calculator</h1><p class=\"lede\">Overall Equipment Effectiveness from one shift of data: availability, performance and quality, plus how many minutes each loss cost you.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"oe-planned\">Planned production time <span class=\"u\">minutes</span></label><input id=\"oe-planned\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"420\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"oe-down\">Unplanned downtime <span class=\"u\">minutes</span></label><input id=\"oe-down\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"47\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"oe-ideal\">Ideal cycle time <span class=\"u\">seconds per unit</span></label><input id=\"oe-ideal\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"1.0\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"oe-total\">Total units produced <span class=\"u\">units</span></label><input id=\"oe-total\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"19271\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"oe-good\">Good units <span class=\"u\">units</span></label><input id=\"oe-good\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"18848\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">OEE</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"oe-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"oe-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"oe-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"oe-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"oe-tbl\"></table><div id=\"oe-pill\"></div></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Run time     = planned time − downtime\nAvailability = run time ÷ planned time\nPerformance  = ideal cycle × total count ÷ run time\nQuality      = good count ÷ total count\nOEE          = availability × performance × quality</code></div><div><h2>What is a good OEE?</h2><p>85% is the commonly quoted world-class benchmark, and many plants run between 40% and 60%. The trend on your own line matters more than the benchmark; the loss breakdown shows where to start.</p></div></div>", "takt-time": "<h1>Takt Time Calculator</h1><p class=\"lede\">The pace a line must run to meet customer demand, the number of stations or operators it needs, and whether your bottleneck can keep up.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"tk-shift\">Shift length <span class=\"u\">minutes</span></label><input id=\"tk-shift\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"480\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"tk-breaks\">Breaks & meetings <span class=\"u\">minutes per shift</span></label><input id=\"tk-breaks\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"50\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"tk-shifts\">Shifts per day <span class=\"u\"></span></label><input id=\"tk-shifts\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"2\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"tk-demand\">Customer demand <span class=\"u\">units per day</span></label><input id=\"tk-demand\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"1200\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"tk-work\">Total work content <span class=\"u\">seconds per unit</span></label><input id=\"tk-work\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"210\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"tk-bottle\">Bottleneck cycle time <span class=\"u\">seconds</span></label><input id=\"tk-bottle\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"45\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">Takt time</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"tk-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"tk-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"tk-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"tk-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"tk-tbl\"></table><div id=\"tk-pill\"></div></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Available time = (shift − breaks) × shifts\nTakt time      = available time ÷ demand\nStations       = work content ÷ takt (round up)\nMax output     = available time ÷ bottleneck cycle</code></div><div><h2>Takt vs cycle time</h2><p>Takt time is set by the customer; cycle time is how fast your process actually runs. If any station's cycle time is longer than takt, that station is a bottleneck and the line cannot meet demand without overtime, an extra shift or rebalancing.</p></div></div>", "pricing": "<h1>Margin &amp; Markup Price Calculator</h1><p class=\"lede\">Set a selling price from your unit cost and target margin, including marketplace or distributor fees, and see the markup that gets you there.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pr-cost\">Unit cost <span class=\"u\">landed / full cost</span></label><input id=\"pr-cost\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"18.4\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pr-margin\">Target gross margin <span class=\"u\">% of price</span></label><input id=\"pr-margin\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"35\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pr-fee\">Channel fee <span class=\"u\">% of price</span></label><input id=\"pr-fee\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"pr-pay\">Payment fee <span class=\"u\">% of price</span></label><input id=\"pr-pay\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"pr-fixed\">Fixed fee per order <span class=\"u\">per unit</span></label><input id=\"pr-fixed\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">Selling price</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"pr-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"pr-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"pr-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"pr-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"pr-tbl\"></table><div id=\"pr-pill\"></div></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Price  = (cost + fixed fee) ÷ (1 − margin − fees)\nMarkup = (price − cost) ÷ cost\nMargin = profit ÷ price</code></div><div><h2>Margin is not markup</h2><p>A 35% markup on cost gives only a 25.9% margin on price. Quoting a markup when the business plan assumes a margin is one of the most common pricing mistakes in small manufacturers.</p></div></div>", "aql": "<h1>AQL Sampling Calculator (ISO 2859-1 / ANSI Z1.4)</h1><p class=\"lede\">How many units to pull from a shipment and how many defects you can accept, for critical, major and minor defects. Enter what you found to get a pass or fail.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"aq-lot\">Lot size <span class=\"u\">units in the order</span></label><input id=\"aq-lot\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"1000\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"aq-level\">Inspection level <span class=\"u\"></span></label><select id=\"aq-level\"><option value=\"1\">I – reduced</option><option value=\"2\" selected>II – normal</option><option value=\"3\">III – tightened</option></select></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"aq-crit\">Critical AQL <span class=\"u\"></span></label><select id=\"aq-crit\"><option value=\"0\" selected>0 (none allowed)</option><option value=\"0.065\">0.065</option><option value=\"0.1\">0.10</option><option value=\"0.25\">0.25</option></select></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"aq-major\">Major AQL <span class=\"u\"></span></label><select id=\"aq-major\"><option value=\"0.065\">0.065</option><option value=\"0.1\">0.10</option><option value=\"0.15\">0.15</option><option value=\"0.25\">0.25</option><option value=\"0.4\">0.40</option><option value=\"0.65\">0.65</option><option value=\"1.0\">1.0</option><option value=\"1.5\">1.5</option><option value=\"2.5\" selected>2.5</option><option value=\"4.0\">4.0</option><option value=\"6.5\">6.5</option></select></div><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"aq-minor\">Minor AQL <span class=\"u\"></span></label><select id=\"aq-minor\"><option value=\"0.065\">0.065</option><option value=\"0.1\">0.10</option><option value=\"0.15\">0.15</option><option value=\"0.25\">0.25</option><option value=\"0.4\">0.40</option><option value=\"0.65\">0.65</option><option value=\"1.0\">1.0</option><option value=\"1.5\">1.5</option><option value=\"2.5\">2.5</option><option value=\"4.0\" selected>4.0</option><option value=\"6.5\">6.5</option></select></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"aq-fc\">Critical found <span class=\"u\">defects</span></label><input id=\"aq-fc\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"0\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"aq-fM\">Major found <span class=\"u\">defects</span></label><input id=\"aq-fM\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"2\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"aq-fm\">Minor found <span class=\"u\">defects</span></label><input id=\"aq-fm\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"3\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">Sample size</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"aq-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"aq-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"aq-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"aq-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"aq-tbl\"></table><div id=\"aq-pill\"></div></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">1. Lot size + level  → code letter (Table 1)\n2. Code letter      → sample size\n3. Code letter + AQL → accept / reject numbers\n   (arrows move to the nearest plan, Table 2-A)\nPass if defects found ≤ accept number</code></div><div><h2>Choosing the AQL</h2><p>Common import inspections use 0 for critical defects, 2.5 for major and 4.0 for minor. Agree the AQLs and the defect list with your supplier before production, not at the inspection.</p></div></div>", "air-leak": "<h1>Compressed Air Leak Cost Calculator</h1><p class=\"lede\">What your compressed air leaks cost each year in electricity, and how fast a leak repair round pays back.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"al-n\">Number of leaks <span class=\"u\"></span></label><input id=\"al-n\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"20\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"al-cfm\">Flow per leak <span class=\"u\">CFM (1 l/s = 2.12 CFM)</span></label><input id=\"al-cfm\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"4.0\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f full\"><div class=\"presets\" data-for=\"al-cfm\"><span>Hole size at ~100 psi:</span><button type=\"button\" data-v=\"1.0\">1/32″</button><button type=\"button\" data-v=\"4.0\">1/16″</button><button type=\"button\" data-v=\"16\">1/8″</button><button type=\"button\" data-v=\"63\">1/4″</button></div></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"al-kw\">Compressor specific power <span class=\"u\">kW per 100 CFM</span></label><input id=\"al-kw\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"20\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"al-hrs\">Operating hours <span class=\"u\">per year</span></label><input id=\"al-hrs\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"6000\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"al-elec\">Electricity price <span class=\"u\">per kWh</span></label><input id=\"al-elec\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"0.12\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"al-fix\">Repair cost <span class=\"u\">per leak</span></label><input id=\"al-fix\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"50\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">Leak cost per year</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"al-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"al-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"al-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"al-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"al-tbl\"></table><div id=\"al-pill\"></div></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Leak flow   = leaks × CFM per leak\nPower       = leak flow × kW per 100 CFM ÷ 100\nEnergy      = power × operating hours\nCost / year = energy × electricity price\nPayback     = repair cost ÷ cost per day</code></div><div><h2>Where the presets come from</h2><p>The hole-size presets are typical flows at about 100 psi (7 bar) for a rounded orifice, based on US Department of Energy compressed air leak tables. Measured flows from an ultrasonic survey are always better than estimates.</p></div></div>", "freight-class": "<h1>LTL Freight Class Calculator (2025 NMFC Density Scale)</h1><p class=\"lede\">Density-based freight class for a pallet or crate under the 13-tier NMFC scale in force since July 19, 2025, compared with the old 11-tier scale.</p><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"fields\"><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"fc-unit\">Units <span class=\"u\"></span></label><select id=\"fc-unit\"><option value=\"in\" selected>inches & pounds</option><option value=\"cm\">centimetres & kilograms</option></select></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"fc-l\">Length <span class=\"u\">per piece</span></label><input id=\"fc-l\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"48\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"fc-w\">Width <span class=\"u\">per piece</span></label><input id=\"fc-w\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"40\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"fc-h\">Height <span class=\"u\">per piece, incl. pallet</span></label><input id=\"fc-h\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"48\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f\"><label for=\"fc-wt\">Weight <span class=\"u\">per piece, incl. pallet</span></label><input id=\"fc-wt\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" value=\"500\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div><div class=\"f full\"><label for=\"fc-n\">Pieces <span class=\"u\">identical pallets / crates</span></label><input id=\"fc-n\" type=\"number\" step=\"1\" value=\"1\" inputmode=\"decimal\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"kicker\">Freight class (2025 scale)</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"fc-out\">–</div><div class=\"sub\" id=\"fc-sub\"></div><div class=\"bar\" id=\"fc-bar\"></div><div class=\"legend\" id=\"fc-leg\"></div><table class=\"bd\" id=\"fc-tbl\"></table><div id=\"fc-pill\"></div></div></div><div class=\"ad\">AD SLOT · 728×90 / responsive</div><div class=\"notes\"><div><h2>How it works</h2><code class=\"fx\">Cubic feet = L × W × H (inches) ÷ 1,728\nDensity    = weight (lb) ÷ cubic feet\nClass      = density band on the NMFC scale</code></div><div><h2>Density only applies to some items</h2><p>The density scale classifies freight that is rated by density in the NMFC. Some commodities have their own item class, and fragile or hard-to-stow freight can be rated differently. Confirm the NMFC item with your carrier before booking.</p></div></div>"}